---
const docsHome = '/azure-sqlvm-toolkit/overview/';
const whyPage = '/azure-sqlvm-toolkit/why-using-azuresqlvmtoolkit/';
const deckPage = '/azure-sqlvm-toolkit/pitch/deck/';
const logoPath = '/azure-sqlvm-toolkit/toolkit-logo.svg';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<meta charset="utf-8" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
		<title>AzureSqlVMToolkit</title>
		<meta
			name="description"
			content="A short pitch for AzureSqlVMToolkit, a PowerShell-first toolkit for repeatable Azure SQL Server VM labs."
		/>
		<style>
			:root {
				color-scheme: dark;
				font-family:
					Inter, ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI",
					sans-serif;
				background: #0b1220;
				color: #e5edf8;
			}

			* {
				box-sizing: border-box;
			}

			body {
				margin: 0;
				min-height: 100vh;
				background:
					linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(14, 165, 233, 0.18), transparent 30rem),
					linear-gradient(315deg, rgba(45, 212, 191, 0.14), transparent 28rem),
					#0b1220;
			}

			main {
				width: min(1120px, calc(100vw - 32px));
				margin: 0 auto;
				padding: 40px 0 56px;
			}

			.hero {
				min-height: 72vh;
			}

			.eyebrow {
				color: #7dd3fc;
				font-size: 0.82rem;
				font-weight: 800;
				letter-spacing: 0.08em;
				text-transform: uppercase;
			}

			h1 {
				margin: 12px 0 18px;
				max-width: 100%;
				font-size: clamp(2.7rem, 5.2vw, 4.9rem);
				line-height: 0.94;
				letter-spacing: 0;
			}

			p {
				color: #cbd5e1;
				font-size: 1.08rem;
				line-height: 1.7;
			}

			.lede {
				max-width: 64ch;
				font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 2vw, 1.45rem);
			}

			.actions {
				display: flex;
				flex-wrap: wrap;
				gap: 12px;
				margin-top: 28px;
			}

			.button {
				display: inline-flex;
				align-items: center;
				justify-content: center;
				min-height: 44px;
				border: 1px solid rgba(125, 211, 252, 0.44);
				border-radius: 8px;
				padding: 10px 16px;
				color: #f8fafc;
				text-decoration: none;
				background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.76);
			}

			.button.primary {
				border-color: #38bdf8;
				background: #0ea5e9;
				color: #06111f;
				font-weight: 800;
			}

			.visual {
				display: grid;
				grid-template-columns: minmax(360px, 1.45fr) minmax(280px, 1fr);
				gap: 28px;
				align-items: center;
				margin-top: 32px;
				border: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.28);
				border-radius: 8px;
				padding: 26px 30px;
				background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.72);
			}

			.logo-lockup {
				display: flex;
				align-items: center;
				justify-content: center;
			}

			.visual-copy {
				display: grid;
				gap: 18px;
			}

			.logo-lockup img {
				width: min(660px, 52vw);
				max-width: 100%;
				height: auto;
			}

			.visual-copy p {
				margin: 0;
			}

			.visual-list {
				display: grid;
				gap: 12px;
				margin: 0;
				padding: 0;
				list-style: none;
			}

			.visual-list li {
				border-top: 1px solid rgba(125, 211, 252, 0.24);
				padding-top: 12px;
				color: #cbd5e1;
			}

			.points {
				display: grid;
				grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
				gap: 16px;
				margin-top: 28px;
			}

			.point {
				border-top: 1px solid rgba(125, 211, 252, 0.36);
				padding-top: 14px;
			}

			.point strong {
				color: #7dd3fc;
			}

			.note {
				margin-top: 32px;
				border-left: 3px solid #38bdf8;
				padding-left: 16px;
				color: #cbd5e1;
			}

			code {
				color: #93c5fd;
			}

			@media (max-width: 860px) {
				.points {
					grid-template-columns: 1fr;
				}

				.hero {
					min-height: auto;
				}

				.visual {
					grid-template-columns: 1fr;
					padding: 24px;
				}

				.logo-lockup img {
					width: min(520px, 90vw);
				}
			}
		</style>
	</head>
	<body>
		<main>
			<section class="hero">
				<div>
					<div class="eyebrow">Azure SQL Server VM labs, with fewer sharp edges</div>
					<h1>AzureSqlVMToolkit</h1>
					<p class="lede">
						A PowerShell-first way to create safer, repeatable Azure SQL Server VM lab
						environments with visible plans, security-minded defaults, and beginner-friendly
						configuration. In the docs and pitch deck, we use <strong>AzSQLVMKit</strong>
						from this point on.
					</p>
					<div class="actions">
						<a class="button primary" href={deckPage}>See pitch deck</a>
						<a class="button" href={whyPage}>Read why it exists</a>
						<a class="button" href={docsHome}>Open toolkit docs</a>
					</div>

					<aside class="visual" aria-label="AzSQLVMKit pitch summary">
						<div class="logo-lockup">
							<img src={logoPath} alt="AzureSqlVMToolkit logo" />
						</div>
						<div class="visual-copy">
							<p>
								<strong>Preview first, deploy second.</strong><br />
								Start with YAML, review the plan, then deploy when the choices are understood.
							</p>
							<ul class="visual-list">
								<li>Build safer SQL Server VM labs without memorizing every Azure resource choice.</li>
								<li>Show generated names, security advice, and VM/storage choices before deployment.</li>
								<li>Use the pitch deck when you want the AzSQLVMKit story in presentation form.</li>
							</ul>
						</div>
					</aside>

					<section class="points" aria-label="Pitch highlights">
						<p class="point">
							<strong>For beginners:</strong><br />
							A short config and clear plan make Azure SQL Server VM concepts easier to see.
						</p>
						<p class="point">
							<strong>For reviewers:</strong><br />
							Networking, naming, secrets, VM image, and storage choices become visible before
							resources exist.
						</p>
						<p class="point">
							<strong>For workshops:</strong><br />
							Repeat the same lab setup across sessions without relying on manual portal memory.
						</p>
					</section>
				</div>
			</section>

			<p class="note">
				The interactive pitch deck is generated from <code>docs-site/pitch.md</code> and is
				published at <a href={deckPage}>/pitch/deck/</a>. While editing the deck locally, run
				<code>npm run slides</code> from <code>docs-site</code>.
			</p>
		</main>
	</body>
</html>
